WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.630
The source says: proposed start,

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.190
subject to approval.

3
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.030
The draft says: we will start.

4
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.490
That small change creates a promise.

5
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.770
Claude's writing can sound convincing,

6
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.490
even when the meaning is wrong.

7
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.650
Your check protects the customer,

8
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.250
and the business.

9
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.230
Before a real task, think about the
people and information involved,

10
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.870
and what could happen
if the draft is wrong.

11
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.270
A small internal reminder and an employment
decision need different levels of

12
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.520
review.

13
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.690
In New Zealand, the Privacy Act
2020 applies whenever you collect,

14
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:41.170
use or share personal information,

15
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.890
and that includes using AI tools.

16
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.770
The Privacy Commissioner's guidance asks
organisations to assess privacy impacts

17
00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.610
before using these tools.

18
00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.150
So keep passwords, client tax records,

19
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:59.110
employee health details and confidential
contracts out of practice chats.

20
00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:02.290
And removing a name may not be enough.

21
00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.570
An address, a unique job title,

22
00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.850
or a mix of facts can
still identify someone.

23
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.050
For practice, invent the whole situation.

24
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.070
Use the fictional examples
in these lessons instead.

25
00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.610
Next, check the evidence.

26
00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:22.530
Compare dates, amounts and
conditions with the original.

27
00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:26.610
Open any cited sources, and
read what they actually say.

28
00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:30.710
Asking a second AI is
not independent proof.

29
00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.110
Check with trusted sources,
and for high-impact work,

30
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.510
the right person reviews
and approves the result.

31
00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.210
New Zealand's public service
guidance says the same:

32
00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:44.170
check results against trusted sources.

33
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.390
A team needs a few usable rules.

34
00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:52.230
Name an owner. State the
approved tool and workspace.

35
00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:55.430
Set data boundaries, and review rules.

36
00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:58.490
And say what happens after a mistake:

37
00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:01.050
who to contact, and how to report it.

38
00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.530
Adapt the policy starter in the lesson,

39
00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.130
then get it approved.

40
00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:08.410
A draft policy isn't approval by itself.

41
00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.550
Now, keep practising.

42
00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.110
The seven-day plan is five minutes a day,

43
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.190
on one task you can check.

44
00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.110
Keep the source, the prompt, the revision,

45
00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.910
and a short check note.

46
00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:24.930
Notice which checks are
easy, and which need help.

47
00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:28.690
Then talk with a colleague or
manager about one useful habit,

48
00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.650
and agree the reviewer
and the data boundary.

49
00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:36.150
That gives you a useful basis
for choosing what to learn next.

50
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
Finish the lessons and quizzes to earn
your completion certificate from The

51
00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.690
Colab. And when you want guided practice,

52
00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:47.730
there are more courses and workshops
at claude training dot co dot N Z,

53
00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.130
slash courses.

54
00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.310
This course is independent training.

55
00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:55.150
Keep the human checks
in your everyday work.
